yunmai-noble
============

The service reads a Bluetooth scale through BlueZ over the system D-Bus.
Make sure the Bluetooth adapter is powered and a scale is in pairing range.

If bluez is installed after this package, add the service user to the
bluetooth group and restart:

  sudo adduser yunmai bluetooth
  sudo systemctl restart yunmai-noble

  systemctl status yunmai-noble
  journalctl -u yunmai-noble -f

Dashboard and API: http://127.0.0.1:3000/
Configuration:     /etc/yunmai-noble/config.toml
Environment:       /etc/yunmai-noble/config.env
Database:          /var/lib/yunmai-noble/historian.sqlite

After editing config.toml or config.env:

  sudo systemctl restart yunmai-noble

The desktop client ships separately as yunmai-noble-desktop. Install
it, or yunmai-noble-full for the service and the client together, to get
the "Yunmai Noble" entry in the application menu.

The web UI is also reachable from other machines on the LAN because the
service binds 0.0.0.0. Change [historian] host in config.toml to
"127.0.0.1" to keep it local.

Run the virtual scale for demos by installing yunmai-noble-simulator.
